{"ref":"BDB Aramaic, רוּם","hw":"רוּם","html":"† <big><big>[<span dir=\"rtl\">רוּם</span>]</big></big>  <strong>vb. rise (</strong>v. BH<strong>)</strong>;—<br><strong>Pe.</strong>  Pf. intr. <span dir=\"rtl\">רִם</span> <a data-ref=\"Daniel 5:20\" href=\"/Daniel.5.20\">Dn 5:20</a> <em>lifted up</em>, of heart, i.e. presumptuous. <strong>Pōʿl.</strong> <em>extol:</em> Pt. <span dir=\"rtl\">מְרוֹמֵם</span> <a data-ref=\"Daniel 4:34\" href=\"/Daniel.4.34\">4:34</a> (<span dir=\"rtl\">ל</span> dei).<br><strong>Haph.</strong>  <em>exalt:</em> Pt. <span dir=\"rtl\">מָרִים</span> <a data-ref=\"Daniel 5:19\" href=\"/Daniel.5.19\">5:19</a> (acc. pers.). <strong>Hithpōʿl.</strong> <em>lift oneself up</em> against, Pf. 2 ms. <span dir=\"rtl\">הִתְרוֹמַמְתָּ</span> <a data-ref=\"Daniel 5:23\" href=\"/Daniel.5.23\">5:23</a> (<span dir=\"rtl\">על</span> dei).","next":"BDB Aramaic, רוּם²","prev":"BDB Aramaic, רֵיחַ"}